<BaseLayout title="GitRacer privacy — cookieless by design" description="What GitRacer stores, how cookieless analytics work, and why the site does not need an analytics cookie banner.">
  <article class="content-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">privacy.txt</span>
    <h1>Useful stats without an analytics identity.</h1>
    <p class="lede">GitRacer runs no analytics, sets no cookies, and builds no visitor profiles. That is why there is no cookie banner.</p>
    <div class="callout">Your theme choice is stored locally in your browser. It is a functional preference, not an advertising or analytics identifier.</div>
    <h2>Public GitHub data</h2>
    <p>The races on this site are saved results built from public GitHub data: handle, display name, profile URL, avatar, contribution years, and public daily contribution totals. Race URLs and their handles are public by design.</p>
    <h2>Avatars</h2>
    <p>Profile pictures load directly from GitHub’s avatar server (<code>avatars.githubusercontent.com</code>), so your browser contacts GitHub when it shows them. GitRacer sends no referrer with those requests.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is static and served by Cloudflare. Cloudflare processes standard request data, such as your IP address, to deliver pages and block abuse. GitRacer keeps no visitor logs or database of its own.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this page: <a href="https://x.com/alexgusevski" rel="me noreferrer">@alexgusevski on X</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
